\ Fast, sauce-independent structural-range regressions.
\ These test exactly the permitted cutlet and month counts.
\ The selection itself is exercised by optional full-calendar tests.
\ They do not require a real Foundation gate search.

To check the cutlet count boundaries:
  Put 6 into the chosen year's span count.
  Prepare the cutlet count range.
  If the cutlet count range's first option is not 6,
    put "A year with six spans may have fewer than six cutlets." into the check report; exit.
  If the cutlet count range's last option is not 6,
    put "A year with six spans may have more than six cutlets." into the check report; exit.
  If the cutlet count range's option count is not 1,
    put "Six spans must permit exactly one cutlet count." into the check report; exit.
  Put 10 into the chosen year's span count.
  Prepare the cutlet count range.
  If the cutlet count range's last option is not 10,
    put "The cutlet upper bound was not limited to the span count." into the check report; exit.
  If the cutlet count range's option count is not 5,
    put "Ten spans should permit five cutlet counts." into the check report; exit.
  Put 18 into the chosen year's span count.
  Prepare the cutlet count range.
  If the cutlet count range's last option is not 17,
    put "The cutlet count exceeded seventeen." into the check report; exit.
  If the cutlet count range's option count is not 12,
    put "A long enough year should permit twelve cutlet counts." into the check report; exit.

To check the month count boundaries:
  Put 252 into the chosen year's year length.
  Prepare the month count range.
  If the month count range's first option is not 3,
    put "The minimum year needs at least three months." into the check report; exit.
  If the month count range's last option is not 47,
    put "The maximum month count for 252 days was wrong." into the check report; exit.
  If the month count range's option count is not 45,
    put "The 252-day month count interval is not 3 through 47." into the check report; exit.
  Put 4244 into the chosen year's year length.
  Prepare the month count range.
  If the month count range's first option is not 35,
    put "A 4244-day year needs at least 35 months." into the check report; exit.
  If the month count range's last option is not 47,
    put "A 4244-day year permits no more than 47 months." into the check report; exit.
  If the month count range's option count is not 13,
    put "The 4244-day month count interval is not 35 through 47." into the check report; exit.
  Put 5778 into the chosen year's year length.
  Prepare the month count range.
  If the month count range's first option is not 47,
    put "The longest year needs 47 months." into the check report; exit.
  If the month count range's last option is not 47,
    put "The longest year may have no more than 47 months." into the check report; exit.
  If the month count range's option count is not 1,
    put "The longest year must have exactly one month-count option." into the check report; exit.
